{"timestamp":"2026-02-02T05:38:54.032Z","tool":"Write","command":"{\"file_path\":\"C:/Users/rasche_j/Documents/workspace/compost-coordinator/SALES.md\",\"content\":\"# Sales Guide\\n\\n## The Opener\\n\\n**\\\"What do you like seeing in your yard?\\\"**\\n\\nListen. Then connect their answer to what we do.\\n\\n| They say... | You say... |\\n|-------------|------------|\\n| Herbs | \\\"We can help your basil actually taste like something\\\" |\\n| Fruit trees | \\\"Fruit trees are hungry - compost is what they need\\\" |\\n| Sunflowers | \\\"You want tall? This is how you get tall\\\" |\\n| Vines | \\\"Those need specific nutrients to look that good\\\" |\\n| Birds/butterflies | \\\"Native plants fed with compost = more pollinators\\\" |\\n| \\\"I don't really garden\\\" | \\\"That's fine - you can gift your share to a neighbor who does\\\" |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Three Strongest Points\\n\\n1. **Your scraps stay local** - Turns into compost 500 feet away, not a landfill 50 miles away\\n\\n2. **You get a soil partner** - We pay attention to your yard, understand your soil, and help you grow what you want\\n\\n3. **You're paying a neighbor kid** - Not a corporation, a local teen building real skills\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Value Prop\\n\\n**Don't say:** \\\"We take your trash\\\"\\n\\n**Say:** \\\"For $25/month you get a soil partner who pays attention to your yard\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Common Objections\\n\\n### \\\"Why would I care where my scraps go?\\\"\\n\\nYour food waste in a landfill creates methane - 20x worse than CO2. One gallon of scraps in your bucket instead of the trash is like taking a 300-mile car trip off the road.\\n\\nBut honestly? Most people don't think about it. Here's what they do notice: no rotting food smell in your trash can all week.\\n\\n### \\\"I don't garden - what would I do with compost?\\\"\\n\\nA few options:\\n- **Houseplants** - herbs, vines, anything green inside\\n- **Gift it** - sponsor a neighbor's garden, it's a great gift\\n- **Skip it** - keep your price the same, we'll sell it to someone who wants it\\n\\nYou're still sequestering carbon either way.\\n\\n### \\\"What if you guys quit halfway through?\\\"\\n\\nIt's a co-op, not one kid. There's always someone to cover. And we're local - if something's wrong, you know exactly where to find us.\\n\\n### \\\"I don't want teenagers on my property every week\\\"\\n\\nWe stay at the curb. Bucket out, bucket back. You don't have to see us.\\n\\n**Invisibility option:** We'll text you before we start our run. Leave your bucket out, we swap it for a clean one that night. Zero interaction if you prefer.\\n\\n### \\\"Is this even a real business?\\\"\\n\\nReal equipment, real training, real accountability. We're just not a corporation taking a cut. Every dollar stays in the neighborhood.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Environmental Close\\n\\n(For people who care about this)\\n\\n\\\"Every gallon you put in that bucket instead of the trash is one less car trip's worth of methane. 300 miles of driving - that's your food scraps rotting in a landfill versus becoming soil here.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Gift Angle\\n\\n\\\"If you don't want the compost yourself, give it to someone who does. Sponsor a neighbor's garden. You choose where it goes. You're still sequestering carbon either way.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Service Pitch\\n\\n\\\"Being a member means your yard gets particular attention. We learn what your soil needs, what you're trying to grow, and how to help. $25/month and your food waste - that's it.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Pricing\\n\\n| Option | Price | Notes |\\n|--------|-------|-------|\\n| Monthly | $25/mo | Try it out |\\n| Annual | $250/yr | Save ~$50, preferred |\\n\\n**What's included:**\\n- Weekly pickup (food scraps, cardboard)\\n- Clean bucket swap\\n- 10 gallons compost/year (or gift to neighbor)\\n- Soil advice when you want it\\n\\n**Payment:** Venmo, Zelle, or card. Cash is tips only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Handling \\\"Maybe Later\\\"\\n\\nGet their contact info. Ask:\\n\\n- \\\"When would be a good time to check back - spring when you're thinking about your garden?\\\"\\n- \\\"Want me to text you when we have our first batch of compost ready? You can see what it looks like.\\\"\\n\\nFollow up once. If no response, move on.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Who to Target First\\n\\n1. **People with gardens visible from the street** - they already care\\n2. **Natural lawns** (no ChemLawn signs) - eco-minded, better materials for us\\n3. **Neighbors you already know** - warm intro beats cold knock\\n4. **Friends' parents** - easy yes to build confidence\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The 30-Second Version\\n\\n\\\"Hi, I'm [name] from the Eagle Crest Compost Co-op. We pick up food scraps and cardboard weekly - you get a clean bucket, we handle everything. $25 a month, and you get free compost for your garden once a year.\\n\\nWhat do you like growing?\\\"\\n\"}","result":"unknown","duration_ms":0}
