{"timestamp":"2026-02-02T15:24:51.358Z","tool":"Task","command":"{\"description\":\"Explore diagram implementation\",\"prompt\":\"Find and analyze the current diagram implementation in the compost-coordinator codebase. I need to understand:\\n\\n1. What framework/library is being used (React Flow, D3, Mermaid, custom canvas, etc.)\\n2. Where the diagram code lives (file paths)\\n3. How nodes and edges are currently defined\\n4. How icons are displayed\\n5. How animation/interaction works currently\\n6. The data structure for the diagram\\n\\nLook for files related to:\\n- Flow/diagram visualization\\n- Node/edge components\\n- Animation/CSS for dotted lines\\n- Icon rendering\\n- Data models for the system map\\n\\nStart with a quick exploration level, focusing on finding the main diagram files and understanding the tech stack.\",\"subagent_type\":\"Explore\"}","result":"unknown","duration_ms":0}
