{"timestamp":"2026-02-02T15:25:48.512Z","tool":"Task","command":"{\"description\":\"Research flow visualization UX\",\"prompt\":\"Research UX patterns and best practices for flow diagram visualization, specifically:\\n\\n1. **Frequency visualization**: How do established flow diagrams (Sankey, process flows, supply chain visualizations) show frequency/cadence of flows? Look for patterns like:\\n   - Line thickness encoding frequency\\n   - Pulse/animation speed variations\\n   - Labels vs visual encoding\\n   - Color gradients for time\\n\\n2. **Icon animation on edges**: Find examples or patterns for showing:\\n   - Multiple icons moving along the same edge\\n   - Bidirectional flows with passing icons\\n   - Layering/z-index strategies when icons overlap\\n   - Animation timing to prevent clutter\\n\\n3. **Edge interaction patterns**: How do interactive diagrams handle:\\n   - Clickable edges vs nodes\\n   - Hover states for edges\\n   - Detail panels for edge data\\n   - Multiple edges between same nodes\\n\\nUse web search to find:\\n- D3.js flow examples\\n- React Flow documentation patterns\\n- Sankey diagram conventions\\n- Supply chain visualization standards\\n- Process flow diagram best practices\\n\\nFocus on finding concrete visual techniques we can adapt to our custom implementation.\",\"subagent_type\":\"Explore\"}","result":"unknown","duration_ms":0}
{"timestamp":"2026-02-02T15:27:49.873Z","tool":"Write","command":"{\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\rasche_j\\\\.claude\\\\plans\\\\snuggly-dreaming-phoenix.md\",\"content\":\"# Implementation Plan: Enhanced Flow Diagram with Animated Icons and Edge Interactions\\n\\n## Overview\\nTransform the current compost coordinator diagram from a node-centric visualization to an **edge-centric flow visualization** where edges show both materials moving AND the work required to move/transform them.\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\n\\n**Tech Stack**: Custom vanilla JS implementation (no framework)\\n- `diagram.js` - Core rendering (264 lines)\\n- `app.js` - Interaction logic (296 lines)\\n- `config.js` - Data models (362 lines)\\n- `styles.css` - Styling & animations (296 lines)\\n\\n**What Exists**:\\n- 11 nodes with icons, positioned via drag-and-drop\\n- 14 edges as animated dotted bezier curves\\n- Click interactions open detail panels for nodes\\n- Edge icons defined in config but NOT rendered\\n\\n**What's Missing**:\\n- Icons animated along edges\\n- Multiple icons per edge (work + material)\\n- Bidirectional edges with passing icons\\n- Clickable edges with detail panels\\n- Edge frequency visualization\\n\\n## Design Decisions\\n\\n### 1. Edge-Centric Model\\n**Nodes = States/Storage locations** (where materials exist)\\n**Edges = Material movement + Work** (transformation/transport)\\n\\nEach edge shows:\\n- **Icon ordering**: Work icon first → output icon(s) second\\n- **Volume data**: Amount flowing through\\n- **Labor data**: Tasks + frequency\\n\\n### 2. Multiple Icons Per Edge\\nUse SVG path animation with staggered timing:\\n- Calculate icon positions using `getPointAtLength()`\\n- Offset animation start times to prevent bunching\\n- Z-index layering for overlap situations\\n\\n### 3. Bidirectional Edge Pattern\\nSingle edge with two \\\"lanes\\\" for icons moving in opposite directions:\\n- Offset icons perpendicular to path direction\\n- One lane for forward flow, one for reverse\\n- Example: Household ↔ Collection (dirty bins out, clean bins return)\\n\\n### 4. Frequency Visualization\\n**Proportional edge width** (primary encoding):\\n- Weekly flows: thicker edges\\n- Monthly flows: medium thickness\\n- Occasional flows: thinner edges\\n\\n**Animation speed** (secondary encoding):\\n- Faster animation = higher frequency\\n- Slower animation = lower frequency\\n\\n**Hover tooltip** shows exact frequency label\\n\\n### 5. Clickable Edges\\nNew interaction layer:\\n- **Hover edge**: Highlight + show tooltip (frequency, material type)\\n- **Click edge**: Open detail panel showing:\\n  - Material flow description\\n  - Volume metrics\\n  - Labor tasks breakdown\\n  - Frequency information\\n\\n### 6. Invisible Junction Points\\nFor converging/diverging flows (e.g., distribution merge point):\\n- No visible node at junction\\n- Edges visually converge at calculated position\\n- Each segment remains independently clickable\\n\\n## Implementation Steps\\n\\n### Phase 1: Data Model Updates (`config.js`)\\n\\n**1.1 Enhance Edge Schema**\\nAdd new fields to edge objects:\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  id: 'edge-id',\\n  from: 'source-node-id',\\n  to: 'target-node-id',\\n  icons: ['🚚', '🍎'],  // Multiple icons: [work, material1, material2, ...]\\n  iconOrder: ['work', 'output'],  // Semantic labels\\n  color: '#22c55e',\\n  frequency: {\\n    value: 1,  // Numeric value\\n    unit: 'weekly',  // 'weekly' | 'monthly' | 'seasonal'\\n    hoursPerPeriod: 16  // Labor hours\\n  },\\n  volume: {\\n    amount: 50,\\n    unit: 'gal/mo'\\n  },\\n  bidirectional: false,  // New: enable for two-way flows\\n  reverseIcons: [],  // Icons for reverse direction (if bidirectional)\\n  strokeWidth: 3,  // Base: 2 (occasional), 3 (monthly), 4 (weekly)\\n  animationDuration: 2  // seconds (lower = faster = more frequent)\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**1.2 Add Edge Click Data**\\nAdd descriptions and task breakdowns:\\n```javascript\\nedges: [\\n  {\\n    id: 'households-collection-food',\\n    from: 'households',\\n    to: 'collection',\\n    icons: ['🚚', '🪣', '🍎'],  // truck (pickup work), bucket, food waste\\n    bidirectional: true,\\n    reverseIcons: ['🪣'],  // clean bucket returns\\n    description: 'Weekly pickup of food waste in 5-gallon buckets',\\n    tasks: [\\n      { name: 'Drive collection route', minPerWeek: 120 },\\n      { name: 'Load/unload bins', minPerWeek: 60 },\\n      { name: 'Clean bins', minPerWeek: 45 }\\n    ],\\n    frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'weekly', hoursPerPeriod: 3.75 },\\n    volume: { amount: 150, unit: 'gal/week' },\\n    strokeWidth: 4,\\n    animationDuration: 1.5\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\n**1.3 Define Junction Points**\\nAdd virtual nodes for invisible merge/split points:\\n```javascript\\njunctionPoints: [\\n  {\\n    id: 'distribution-merge',\\n    position: { x: 0.75, y: 0.60 },\\n    visible: false  // Don't render as node\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\n### Phase 2: SVG Icon Animation System (`diagram.js`)\\n\\n**2.1 Create Icon Animation Function**\\nAdd new function to animate icons along paths:\\n\\n```javascript\\n/**\\n * Animates icons along an SVG path using CSS animations\\n * @param {SVGPathElement} path - The edge path element\\n * @param {Array} icons - Array of icon strings ['🚚', '🍎']\\n * @param {number} duration - Animation duration in seconds\\n * @param {boolean} bidirectional - Enable reverse lane\\n * @param {Array} reverseIcons - Icons for reverse direction\\n */\\nfunction animateIconsOnPath(path, icons, duration, bidirectional = false, reverseIcons = []) {\\n  const edgeId = path.id;\\n  const pathLength = path.getTotalLength();\\n\\n  // Forward direction icons\\n  icons.forEach((icon, index) => {\\n    const iconEl = createPathIcon(icon, edgeId, index, 'forward');\\n    const offset = (index / icons.length) * duration;  // Stagger timing\\n    animateIconAlongPath(iconEl, path, pathLength, duration, offset, 0);  // lane 0 = center\\n  });\\n\\n  // Reverse direction icons (if bidirectional)\\n  if (bidirectional && reverseIcons.length > 0) {\\n    reverseIcons.forEach((icon, index) => {\\n      const iconEl = createPathIcon(icon, edgeId, index, 'reverse');\\n      const offset = (index / reverseIcons.length) * duration;\\n      animateIconAlongPath(iconEl, path, pathLength, duration, offset, 10);  // lane offset 10px\\n    });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction createPathIcon(icon, edgeId, index, direction) {\\n  const iconEl = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'text');\\n  iconEl.classList.add('flow-icon');\\n  iconEl.setAttribute('id', `${edgeId}-icon-${direction}-${index}`);\\n  iconEl.textContent = icon;\\n  iconEl.setAttribute('font-size', '1.2rem');\\n  iconEl.setAttribute('text-anchor', 'middle');\\n  document.getElementById('edges').appendChild(iconEl);\\n  return iconEl;\\n}\\n\\nfunction animateIconAlongPath(iconEl, path, pathLength, duration, startDelay, laneOffset) {\\n  let startTime = null;\\n\\n  function animate(timestamp) {\\n    if (!startTime) startTime = timestamp + (startDelay * 1000);\\n    const elapsed = timestamp - startTime;\\n    const progress = (elapsed / (duration * 1000)) % 1;  // Loop 0-1\\n\\n    const distance = progress * pathLength;\\n    const point = path.getPointAtLength(distance);\\n\\n    // Calculate perpendicular offset for lane\\n    let offsetX = 0, offsetY = 0;\\n    if (laneOffset !== 0) {\\n      const nextPoint = path.getPointAtLength(Math.min(distance + 1, pathLength));\\n      const angle = Math.atan2(nextPoint.y - point.y, nextPoint.x - point.x);\\n      offsetX = -Math.sin(angle) * laneOffset;\\n      offsetY = Math.cos(angle) * laneOffset;\\n    }\\n\\n    iconEl.setAttribute('x', point.x + offsetX);\\n    iconEl.setAttribute('y', point.y + offsetY);\\n\\n    requestAnimationFrame(animate);\\n  }\\n\\n  requestAnimationFrame(animate);\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**2.2 Integrate into Rendering Pipeline**\\nModify `renderEdges()` to call animation after path creation:\\n\\n```javascript\\nfunction renderEdges() {\\n  const svg = document.getElementById('edges');\\n  svg.innerHTML = '';  // Clear existing\\n\\n  edges.forEach(edge => {\\n    const path = createEdgePath(edge);  // Existing bezier path creation\\n\\n    // Apply frequency-based styling\\n    path.style.strokeWidth = `${edge.strokeWidth}px`;\\n    path.style.animationDuration = `${edge.animationDuration}s`;\\n\\n    svg.appendChild(path);\\n\\n    // Animate icons on path\\n    if (edge.icons && edge.icons.length > 0) {\\n      animateIconsOnPath(\\n        path,\\n        edge.icons,\\n        edge.animationDuration,\\n        edge.bidirectional,\\n        edge.reverseIcons || []\\n      );\\n    }\\n  });\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**2.3 Add Edge Width Encoding**\\nUpdate `createEdgePath()` to use frequency-based width:\\n\\n```javascript\\nfunction createEdgePath(edge) {\\n  const path = document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg', 'path');\\n  path.setAttribute('id', `edge-${edge.id}`);\\n  path.setAttribute('class', 'edge animated');\\n  path.setAttribute('d', generateBezierPath(edge));\\n  path.setAttribute('stroke', edge.color);\\n  path.setAttribute('stroke-width', edge.strokeWidth || 2);\\n  path.setAttribute('fill', 'none');\\n\\n  // Store edge data for click handling\\n  path.dataset.edgeId = edge.id;\\n\\n  return path;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Phase 3: Edge Click Interactions (`app.js`)\\n\\n**3.1 Add Edge Click Listeners**\\nCreate new event delegation for edges:\\n\\n```javascript\\n// Add to initApp()\\nconst edgesLayer = document.getElementById('edges');\\nedgesLayer.addEventListener('click', handleEdgeClick);\\nedgesLayer.addEventListener('mouseenter', handleEdgeHover, true);\\nedgesLayer.addEventListener('mouseleave', handleEdgeLeave, true);\\n\\nfunction handleEdgeClick(e) {\\n  const path = e.target.closest('path.edge');\\n  if (!path) return;\\n\\n  const edgeId = path.dataset.edgeId;\\n  const edge = edges.find(e => e.id === edgeId);\\n  if (edge) {\\n    showEdgeDetail(edge);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction handleEdgeHover(e) {\\n  const path = e.target.closest('path.edge');\\n  if (!path) return;\\n\\n  path.classList.add('edge-hover');\\n  const edge = edges.find(e => e.id === path.dataset.edgeId);\\n  if (edge) {\\n    showEdgeTooltip(edge, e.clientX, e.clientY);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction handleEdgeLeave(e) {\\n  const path = e.target.closest('path.edge');\\n  if (!path) return;\\n\\n  path.classList.remove('edge-hover');\\n  hideEdgeTooltip();\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**3.2 Create Edge Detail Panel**\\nNew function to display edge information:\\n\\n```javascript\\nfunction showEdgeDetail(edge) {\\n  const panel = document.getElementById('detail-panel');\\n  const iconStr = edge.icons.join(' ');\\n\\n  const tasksHTML = edge.tasks ? edge.tasks.map(task => {\\n    const timeLabel = task.minPerWeek\\n      ? `${task.minPerWeek} min/week`\\n      : `${task.minPerMonth} min/month`;\\n    return `<li>${task.name}: ${timeLabel}</li>`;\\n  }).join('') : '';\\n\\n  panel.innerHTML = `\\n    <div class=\\\"detail-header\\\">\\n      <div class=\\\"detail-icon\\\">${iconStr}</div>\\n      <div class=\\\"detail-title\\\">Material Flow</div>\\n      <button class=\\\"close-btn\\\">&times;</button>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"detail-content\\\">\\n      <p>${edge.description || 'Material and work flowing between stages'}</p>\\n\\n      <div class=\\\"detail-section\\\">\\n        <h4>Flow Details</h4>\\n        <p><strong>Frequency:</strong> ${edge.frequency.value} ${edge.frequency.unit}</p>\\n        <p><strong>Volume:</strong> ${edge.volume.amount} ${edge.volume.unit}</p>\\n        ${edge.bidirectional ? '<p><strong>Type:</strong> Bidirectional flow</p>' : ''}\\n      </div>\\n\\n      ${edge.tasks ? `\\n        <div class=\\\"detail-section\\\">\\n          <h4>Work Required</h4>\\n          <ul class=\\\"task-list\\\">${tasksHTML}</ul>\\n          <p class=\\\"total-time\\\">Total: ${edge.frequency.hoursPerPeriod} hours/${edge.frequency.unit}</p>\\n        </div>\\n      ` : ''}\\n    </div>\\n  `;\\n\\n  panel.classList.add('visible');\\n\\n  panel.querySelector('.close-btn').addEventListener('click', () => {\\n    panel.classList.remove('visible');\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nfunction showEdgeTooltip(edge, x, y) {\\n  let tooltip = document.getElementById('edge-tooltip');\\n  if (!tooltip) {\\n    tooltip = document.createElement('div');\\n    tooltip.id = 'edge-tooltip';\\n    tooltip.className = 'edge-tooltip';\\n    document.body.appendChild(tooltip);\\n  }\\n\\n  tooltip.innerHTML = `\\n    <div><strong>${edge.icons.join(' ')}</strong></div>\\n    <div>${edge.frequency.value} ${edge.frequency.unit}</div>\\n  `;\\n\\n  tooltip.style.left = `${x + 10}px`;\\n  tooltip.style.top = `${y + 10}px`;\\n  tooltip.style.display = 'block';\\n}\\n\\nfunction hideEdgeTooltip() {\\n  const tooltip = document.getElementById('edge-tooltip');\\n  if (tooltip) {\\n    tooltip.style.display = 'none';\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Phase 4: CSS Enhancements (`styles.css`)\\n\\n**4.1 Edge Hover States**\\n```css\\n.edge {\\n  cursor: pointer;\\n  transition: stroke-opacity 0.2s, stroke-width 0.2s;\\n}\\n\\n.edge:hover,\\n.edge.edge-hover {\\n  stroke-opacity: 1;\\n  stroke-width: calc(var(--edge-width) * 1.3);  /* Thicken on hover */\\n}\\n\\n.edge.animated {\\n  stroke-dasharray: 8 4;\\n  animation: flow var(--animation-duration, 2s) linear infinite;\\n}\\n\\n@keyframes flow {\\n  from { stroke-dashoffset: 12; }\\n  to { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**4.2 Flow Icon Styling**\\n```css\\n.flow-icon {\\n  pointer-events: none;  /* Don't block edge clicks */\\n  user-select: none;\\n  font-size: 1.2rem;\\n  opacity: 0.9;\\n}\\n\\n/* Z-index layering for overlaps */\\nsvg .flow-icon {\\n  z-index: 100;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**4.3 Edge Tooltip**\\n```css\\n.edge-tooltip {\\n  position: fixed;\\n  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);\\n  color: white;\\n  padding: 8px 12px;\\n  border-radius: 6px;\\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\\n  pointer-events: none;\\n  z-index: 10000;\\n  display: none;\\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\\n}\\n\\n.edge-tooltip div {\\n  margin: 2px 0;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**4.4 Frequency-Based Width Variables**\\nAdd CSS custom properties for dynamic width:\\n```css\\n.edge[data-frequency=\\\"weekly\\\"] {\\n  --edge-width: 4px;\\n  --animation-duration: 1.5s;\\n}\\n\\n.edge[data-frequency=\\\"monthly\\\"] {\\n  --edge-width: 3px;\\n  --animation-duration: 2.5s;\\n}\\n\\n.edge[data-frequency=\\\"seasonal\\\"] {\\n  --edge-width: 2px;\\n  --animation-duration: 4s;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Phase 5: Rebuild Edge Data (`config.js`)\\n\\n**5.1 Collection Flow (Bidirectional)**\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  id: 'households-collection-food',\\n  from: 'households',\\n  to: 'collection',\\n  icons: ['🚚', '🪣', '🍎'],  // pickup truck, bucket, food waste\\n  bidirectional: true,\\n  reverseIcons: ['🪣'],  // clean bucket returns\\n  description: 'Weekly pickup of food waste in 5-gallon buckets',\\n  tasks: [\\n    { name: 'Drive collection route', minPerWeek: 120 },\\n    { name: 'Load/unload buckets', minPerWeek: 60 }\\n  ],\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'weekly', hoursPerPeriod: 3 },\\n  volume: { amount: 150, unit: 'gal/week' },\\n  color: '#22c55e',\\n  strokeWidth: 4,\\n  animationDuration: 1.5\\n},\\n\\n{\\n  id: 'households-collection-cardboard',\\n  from: 'households',\\n  to: 'collection',\\n  icons: ['🚚', '📦'],  // Same pickup, cardboard boxes\\n  description: 'Weekly pickup of cardboard (shared route with food waste)',\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'weekly', hoursPerPeriod: 0 },  // 0 = shared labor\\n  volume: { amount: 50, unit: 'boxes/week' },\\n  color: '#f59e0b',\\n  strokeWidth: 4,\\n  animationDuration: 1.5\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**5.2 Processing Flows (Transformation)**\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  id: 'collection-browns-cardboard',\\n  from: 'collection',\\n  to: 'cardboard',\\n  icons: ['✂️', '📄'],  // Shredding work → shredded cardboard\\n  description: 'Cardboard shredding and storage',\\n  tasks: [\\n    { name: 'Shred cardboard', minPerWeek: 45 },\\n    { name: 'Store in browns pile', minPerWeek: 15 }\\n  ],\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'weekly', hoursPerPeriod: 1 },\\n  volume: { amount: 50, unit: 'boxes/week' },\\n  color: '#f59e0b',\\n  strokeWidth: 3,\\n  animationDuration: 2\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**5.3 Stage Transitions (Biological Work)**\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  id: 'stage1-stage2',\\n  from: 'stage1',\\n  to: 'stage2',\\n  icons: ['👷', '🪱', '🦠', '🌡️'],  // Human labor, worms, microbes, heat\\n  description: 'Monthly pile turning + continuous decomposition',\\n  tasks: [\\n    { name: 'Turn pile', minPerMonth: 60 },\\n    { name: 'Monitor temperature', minPerMonth: 30 }\\n  ],\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'monthly', hoursPerPeriod: 1.5 },\\n  volume: { amount: 200, unit: 'gal/month' },\\n  color: '#22c55e',\\n  strokeWidth: 3,\\n  animationDuration: 3\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**5.4 Distribution (Converge then Split)**\\n```javascript\\n// Add junction point to config\\nconst junctionPoints = [\\n  { id: 'distribution', position: { x: 0.77, y: 0.62 }, visible: false }\\n];\\n\\n// Edges to junction\\n{\\n  id: 'stage4-distribution',\\n  from: 'stage4',\\n  to: 'distribution',\\n  icons: ['🪱', '🫖'],  // Harvest output\\n  description: 'Harvested vermicompost ready for distribution',\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'monthly', hoursPerPeriod: 0 },\\n  volume: { amount: 200, unit: 'gal/month' },\\n  color: '#22c55e',\\n  strokeWidth: 3,\\n  animationDuration: 2.5\\n},\\n\\n{\\n  id: 'tea-distribution',\\n  from: 'tea',\\n  to: 'distribution',\\n  icons: ['🫖', '💧'],  // Brew work → worm tea\\n  description: 'Brewed worm tea ready for distribution',\\n  tasks: [\\n    { name: 'Brew worm tea', minPerMonth: 120 },\\n    { name: 'Bottle and store', minPerMonth: 30 }\\n  ],\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'monthly', hoursPerPeriod: 2.5 },\\n  volume: { amount: 20, unit: 'gal/month' },\\n  color: '#06b6d4',\\n  strokeWidth: 3,\\n  animationDuration: 2.5\\n},\\n\\n// Edges from junction (now both icons present)\\n{\\n  id: 'distribution-households',\\n  from: 'distribution',\\n  to: 'households',\\n  icons: ['🚚', '💧', '🫖'],  // Delivery work → both products\\n  description: 'Monthly delivery to households (compost returns program)',\\n  tasks: [\\n    { name: 'Load delivery truck', minPerMonth: 30 },\\n    { name: 'Deliver to households', minPerMonth: 120 }\\n  ],\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'monthly', hoursPerPeriod: 2.5 },\\n  volume: { amount: 100, unit: 'gal compost + tea/month' },\\n  color: '#6366f1',\\n  strokeWidth: 3,\\n  animationDuration: 2.5\\n},\\n\\n{\\n  id: 'distribution-purchasers',\\n  from: 'distribution',\\n  to: 'purchasers',\\n  icons: ['🚚', '💰', '💧', '🫖'],  // Delivery work → payment → both products\\n  description: 'Monthly delivery to customers (paid orders)',\\n  tasks: [\\n    { name: 'Load delivery truck', minPerMonth: 30 },\\n    { name: 'Deliver to customers', minPerMonth: 180 }\\n  ],\\n  frequency: { value: 1, unit: 'monthly', hoursPerPeriod: 3.5 },\\n  volume: { amount: 120, unit: 'gal compost + tea/month' },\\n  color: '#ec4899',\\n  strokeWidth: 3,\\n  animationDuration: 2.5\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Phase 6: Junction Point Rendering (`diagram.js`)\\n\\n**6.1 Add Junction Point Support**\\n```javascript\\nfunction getNodePosition(nodeId) {\\n  // Check if it's a junction point\\n  const junction = junctionPoints.find(j => j.id === nodeId);\\n  if (junction) {\\n    return junction.position;\\n  }\\n\\n  // Otherwise use existing node position logic\\n  const saved = localStorage.getItem('compost-positions');\\n  // ... existing code\\n}\\n\\nfunction renderJunctionPoints() {\\n  // Only render if debugging mode is enabled\\n  if (!window.DEBUG_JUNCTIONS) return;\\n\\n  junctionPoints.forEach(junction => {\\n    const div = document.createElement('div');\\n    div.className = 'junction-point';\\n    div.style.left = `${junction.position.x * 100}%`;\\n    div.style.top = `${junction.position.y * 100}%`;\\n    div.textContent = '⊕';\\n    document.getElementById('nodes-layer').appendChild(div);\\n  });\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**6.2 Debug Mode for Junction Visibility**\\nAdd to `app.js`:\\n```javascript\\n// Enable junction debugging with Ctrl+J\\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\\n  if (e.ctrlKey && e.key === 'j') {\\n    window.DEBUG_JUNCTIONS = !window.DEBUG_JUNCTIONS;\\n    renderDiagram();\\n  }\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## Testing & Verification\\n\\n### Visual Verification\\n1. **Icon Movement**:\\n   - Icons should flow smoothly along paths\\n   - Multiple icons maintain consistent spacing\\n   - Bidirectional flows show icons passing each other without overlap\\n\\n2. **Frequency Encoding**:\\n   - Weekly flows (households ↔ collection) are thickest and fastest\\n   - Monthly flows (stage transitions) are medium thickness and moderate speed\\n   - Seasonal flows are thinnest and slowest\\n\\n3. **Junction Points**:\\n   - Distribution merge: tea and compost flows converge visually\\n   - After merge: both icons (💧 🫖) appear on outgoing edges\\n   - No visible node at junction (unless debug mode enabled)\\n\\n### Interaction Verification\\n1. **Edge Hover**:\\n   - Hover shows tooltip with frequency and icons\\n   - Edge thickens slightly on hover\\n   - Cursor changes to pointer\\n\\n2. **Edge Click**:\\n   - Click opens detail panel\\n   - Panel shows material description, frequency, volume, tasks\\n   - Panel can be closed via X button, Escape key, or click outside\\n\\n3. **Node Click** (should still work):\\n   - Existing node detail panels remain functional\\n   - Edge clicks don't interfere with node clicks\\n\\n### Performance Verification\\n1. **Animation Smoothness**:\\n   - All icons animate at 60fps (use Chrome DevTools performance tab)\\n   - No jank during window resize\\n   - Drag-and-drop remains responsive\\n\\n2. **Memory**:\\n   - No memory leaks from animation loops (check with Performance Monitor)\\n   - RequestAnimationFrame properly cleanup on rerender\\n\\n### Data Accuracy\\n1. **Labor Hours**:\\n   - Edge task times sum correctly\\n   - Shared logistics (collection route) doesn't double-count labor\\n   - Monthly totals match expectations\\n\\n2. **Volume Flows**:\\n   - Input volumes (households) balance output volumes (purchasers)\\n   - Stage transitions account for decomposition losses\\n   - Tea brewing volumes realistic relative to inputs\\n\\n## Rollback Plan\\nIf performance issues or visual clutter:\\n1. Reduce icons per edge (keep only material, remove work icons)\\n2. Disable continuous animation (static icons at midpoint)\\n3. Revert to node-centric model with edge labels only\\n\\n## Future Enhancements (Out of Scope)\\n- Zoom/pan functionality for complex flows\\n- Real-time data binding (live volume updates)\\n- Edge filtering by material type\\n- Timeline scrubbing (show flows at different time periods)\\n- Export to CSV/JSON for external analysis\\n\\n## Critical Files to Modify\\n\\n| File | Changes | Lines Affected |\\n|------|---------|----------------|\\n| `config.js` | Enhance edge schema, add junction points, rebuild all edge data | ~100-200 lines |\\n| `diagram.js` | Add icon animation system, junction rendering, edge width encoding | ~150-200 new lines |\\n| `app.js` | Add edge click handlers, edge detail panel, tooltip system | ~100-150 new lines |\\n| `styles.css` | Edge hover states, tooltip styles, flow icon styles | ~50-80 new lines |\\n\\n**Total estimated additions**: ~400-600 lines of code\\n**Refactoring**: Minimal (mostly additive changes)\\n\\n## Implementation Order\\n1. **Phase 1**: Data model (safest, no visual changes)\\n2. **Phase 4**: CSS first (test hover states without full implementation)\\n3. **Phase 2**: Icon animation (core visual feature)\\n4. **Phase 3**: Edge interactions (builds on Phase 2)\\n5. **Phase 5**: Rebuild edge data (makes everything meaningful)\\n6. **Phase 6**: Junction points (final polish)\\n\"}","result":"unknown","duration_ms":0}
